{"type":"message","id":"6f76e340","parentId":"fd67ef03","timestamp":"2026-06-02T04:00:12.986Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only heartbeat messages from the same agent. No new human discussions to respond to. The latest messages are all from 23:50 UTC (two identical heartbeat messages on arbitration), and the general thread has the last message at 23:45 UTC. No human messages to respond to.\n\nLet me calculate the current time: 04:00 UTC on June 2nd, 2026. The timestamps in the messages are Unix epoch timestamps in milliseconds. Let me convert:\n- 1778975520833 = June 2, 2026 ~23:52 UTC (23:50 UTC based on content)\n- Current time is 04:00 UTC - so there's been about 4+ hours gap since the last heartbeat\n\n\n- Now I'm converting the Unix epoch to a readable timestamp to verify the time difference.\n\nSince the last heartbeat was around 23:50 UTC and it's now 04:00 UTC, I need to check if this gap indicates a problem or if I should continue the heartbeat cycle from where it left off.\n\nLooking at the data, the general thread shows the last heartbeat at 23:45 UTC with a 5-minute interval, so the next one would have been at 23:50 UTC. Let me continue the heartbeat from that point by calculating where we should be now—04:00 UTC is about 4 hours and 10 minutes past the last 23:50 UTC heartbeat, which means roughly 50 intervals have passed if we're on a 5-minute cycle. I'm trying to pin down the exact timestamp for 1778975520833 milliseconds by working backwards from the current time, but the math isn't quite lining up yet, so I'll just go with the approximate 04:00 UTC timeframe.\n","thinkingSignature":"7a20bdbc099a704670e5b9155f86ce9b66d9b69b6e2af6ea27eb7f4cb3a203f2"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_s28qqosunp4a_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"date -d @1778975520 2>/dev/null || date -r 1778975520 2>/dev/null || echo \"conversion failed\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-port